  "source_notes": "Extracted 2026-07-13 via Playwright from https://siphoxhealth.com/partner/test-panels (B2B partner page with expandable 'View All N Markers' buttons per panel card -- clicked each of the 5 panel cards and read the expanded card text directly, all 5 expansions succeeded on first click, no failures). Gender-qualified markers (e.g. 'Testosterone, Total (Males)') are kept as separate raw marker strings with the qualifier preserved.\n\nPRICING CORRECTION vs. pre-existing DB: the DB's pre-migration vendor_tiers had Core:$99, Heart & Metabolic:$125, Hormone Focus:$125, Thyroid Focus:$125, Ultimate 360:$225 -- these are now STALE. Checked the live consumer /pricing/<program> pages (not the partner page) and found all four standalone focus panels (Core/Longevity Essentials, Hormone, Thyroid, Heart & Metabolic) uniformly priced at $124 ('Included with membership (only $124)' appears identically on all four pages), and Ultimate 360 explicitly computed on its own page as '$124 membership + $125 upgrade' = $249. Used these live $124/$249 prices as canonical here instead of the stale DB tier prices.\n\nEXCLUDED: each pricing page also offers combo upsell add-ons (e.g. 'Hormone+' +$50 on the core-program page, 'Wellness & Hormone+' +$75 on the heart-and-metabolic page) that combine two focus areas at a discount off buying both separately. These showed inconsistent naming and pricing across pages (not clearly the same product), and their exact combined marker composition isn't independently itemized anywhere -- excluded from this catalog pending a follow-up pass, same treatment as Marek's and Vitals Vault's checkout-only/unclear add-ons.\n\nSUPERSET CHECK: Ultimate Health Panel (62 markers) is NEARLY but not exactly a superset of the union of the other 4 panels (57 unique base markers). It's missing 'Female Free Androgen Index (FAI)' (Hormone Focus has this gender-specific variant; Ultimate instead has a single unified 'Free Androgen Index (FAI)' with no gender qualifier) and adds 6 markers not found in any other panel: Vitamin B12, Iron, Iron Saturation, Iron Bind. Cap. (TIBC), Unsaturated iron-binding capacity test (UIBC), Folate. So Ultimate is its own separately-curated 62-marker set, not a strict superset -- correct to seed as its own independent product (which this does).",
